{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdqfDxKfuYoMRVHgBagqy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan to Wire `check:pricing-sync` into Pre-commit Hook\n\n1. **Check if a pre-commit hook already exists**\n   - Look at `.git/hooks/pre-commit` (or `.husky/pre-commit` if using husky)\n   - Note whether the file exists and what it currently contains\n\n2. **Verify the check script works**\n   - Run `npm run check:pricing-sync` once to confirm it exits 0 on current state\n   - This confirms the script is functional before blocking commits with it\n\n3. **Add the check to the pre-commit hook**\n   - If using **husky** (most common): edit `.husky/pre-commit` and add `npm run check:pricing-sync` as a new line before the final exit\n   - If using **git hooks directly**: edit `.git/hooks/pre-commit` to include the same command\n   - If no hook exists: create one with proper shebang (`#!/bin/sh`), add the command, make it executable (`chmod +x`)\n\n4. **Make it blocking**\n   - Ensure the hook exits with the check's exit code (don't suppress it with `||`)\n   - Structure: `npm run check:pricing-sync || exit 1` (or just rely on the script's native exit code)\n\n5. **Test the hook locally**\n   - Make a small edit to `src/pricing/tiers.ts` without updating `docs/pricing-table.md`\n   - Attempt to commit—verify the hook blocks it with the check's error output\n   - Revert the edit and commit again—verify it succeeds\n\n6. **Commit the hook changes**\n   - Stage the hook file itself (`.husky/pre-commit` or equivalent) and push\n   - Document in the commit message that this is now a blocking check"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":419,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
